(4069967, 581300, 62671, '<td valign="top">I love that you did a still life image.  These are not as popular at the moment.  I love the lighting on the fruit and dishes.  Not so fond of the hot spot on the cotton ''rag'' I feel that fabric should be a more sensual fabric. <br/>The background has some great textures  but the seam lines draw my eye.  The colors of the image is great, but I would perfer to see the tapestry on the background and a deep rich wood tone or marble surface.   The styles of the dishes is a hodgepodge.  The pitcher has an aztec feel, the vase is oriental in nature and the plate (from this angle) looks like a french.  I would like the dishes to be more along the same styling.   I also love the unopened flowers in the vase. they have some great shape and color.   They lend some hight to the left side, which is good.  The formation of the fruit brings your eye down at an angle, that is also good.  The pitcher though adds height to the right side.  That is distressful to the flow of the image.  I would prefer the pitcher in the left side forming a diagonal line visually.<br/> <br/>Just my opinion and possibly some pointers.  Great job on the shot!</td>', 'I love that you did a still life image.  These are not as popular at the moment.  I love the lighting on the fruit and dishes.  Not so fond of the hot spot on the cotton ''rag'' I feel that fabric should be a more sensual fabric. The background has some great textures  but the seam lines draw my eye.  The colors of the image is great, but I would perfer to see the tapestry on the background and a deep rich wood tone or marble surface.   The styles of the dishes is a hodgepodge.  The pitcher has an aztec feel, the vase is oriental in nature and the plate (from this angle) looks like a french.  I would like the dishes to be more along the same styling.   I also love the unopened flowers in the vase. they have some great shape and color.   They lend some hight to the left side, which is good.  The formation of the fruit brings your eye down at an angle, that is also good.  The pitcher though adds height to the right side.  That is distressful to the flow of the image.  I would prefer the pitcher in the left side forming a diagonal line visually. Just my opinion and possibly some pointers.  Great job on the shot!', '2007-09-07 18:28:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4069984, 582956, 62671, '<td valign="top">What a lovely idea!  Each of the petals resemble a brush stroke!  Well done!</td>', 'What a lovely idea!  Each of the petals resemble a brush stroke!  Well done!', '2007-09-07 18:35:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4069991, 580194, 62671, '<td valign="top">Excellent still life.   I love the drapey background,  the colors are very striking.  The scale of the flowers feels a bit small to me.  and the chest is to dark.  I would love to see some wine bottles poking out of the cavity.</td>', 'Excellent still life.   I love the drapey background,  the colors are very striking.  The scale of the flowers feels a bit small to me.  and the chest is to dark.  I would love to see some wine bottles poking out of the cavity.', '2007-09-07 18:38:24.000000', NULL, 1),
